Subject: [PATCH] Fix Pulse shutdown hang on SIGTERM (graceful, interruptible sleep)

Re-cut for LifeOS 7.1.1 (was the v5.0.0 patch 0029). Upstream relocated the
daemon: PAI/PULSE/pulse.ts -> LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts, and the
sleep cap changed (90s -> MAX_SLEEP_MS = 60_000). The entry point is pulse.ts:
the systemd .service (ExecStart=bun run pulse.ts, TimeoutStopSec=5), the
launchd .plist (ProgramArguments: bun run pulse.ts) and manage.sh all exec it.

Problem: on shutdown, systemd/launchd sends SIGTERM. pulse.ts registers a
SIGTERM handler, but it only sets `shuttingDown = true`. The main loop is
normally parked in `await Bun.sleep(sleepMs)` (sleepMs up to MAX_SLEEP_MS =
60_000ms), and setting the flag does not interrupt that sleep — the loop only
re-checks `while (!shuttingDown)` once the sleep elapses. So the daemon hangs
up to 60s; under systemd (TimeoutStopSec=5) it is SIGKILLed mid-operation,
skipping writeState/cleanup.

Root cause: the shutdown signal cannot wake a parked Bun.sleep.

Fix (graceful, code-only — deliberately NOT a systemd TimeoutStopSec net):
  - shutdown() calls wakeFromSleep() to interrupt the parked sleep.
  - the main-loop sleep becomes an interruptible Promise (clearTimeout +
    resolve on signal) so on SIGTERM/SIGINT the loop wakes immediately, runs
    the existing cleanup (server.stop, module stops, writeState) and returns.
  - a final process.exit(0) after cleanup guarantees prompt exit even if a
    module leaves a live handle.

Result: shutdown completes in well under a second, cleanly, instead of a
60s hang / mid-operation SIGKILL.

Scope: touches only pulse.ts (the file that actually runs). The unreferenced
pulse-unified.ts / pulse-old.ts variants are left untouched (dead code — no
.service/.plist/manage.sh/test execs them).

Generated via `diff -u` against pristine 7.1.1 src (never hand-counted hunks).
--- a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
+++ b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
@@ -542,11 +542,13 @@
 
   // Graceful shutdown
   let shuttingDown = false
+  let wakeFromSleep: () => void = () => {}
   const isShuttingDown = () => shuttingDown
   const shutdown = () => {
     if (shuttingDown) return
     shuttingDown = true
     log("info", "Shutting down gracefully")
+    wakeFromSleep() // interrupt the long Bun.sleep in the main loop so cleanup runs at once (else systemd waits TimeoutStopSec then SIGKILLs)
   }
   process.on("SIGTERM", shutdown)
   process.on("SIGINT", shutdown)
@@ -956,7 +958,14 @@
     const sleepMs = Math.max(MIN_SLEEP_MS, Math.min(nextDueMs - elapsed, MAX_SLEEP_MS))
 
     if (!shuttingDown) {
-      await Bun.sleep(sleepMs)
+      // interruptible sleep: SIGTERM/SIGINT wakes it immediately (else the loop parks up to MAX_SLEEP_MS)
+      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
+        const timer = setTimeout(resolve, sleepMs)
+        wakeFromSleep = () => {
+          clearTimeout(timer)
+          resolve()
+        }
+      })
     }
   }
 
@@ -968,6 +977,7 @@
   if (syslogModule) await syslogModule.stop?.()
   await writeState(STATE_PATH, state).catch(() => {})
   log("info", "LifeOS Pulse stopped", { uptimeMs: Date.now() - state.startedAt })
+  process.exit(0) // after graceful cleanup, guarantee exit even if a module leaves a live handle
 }
 
 main().catch((err) => {
